## Problem (tree truth)
Wave-2 asked for a **rebuilt host**. Wave-3 peers re-proved the same 04:49
ELF (`s29c_peer1.oot` **REJECT** 3/4; `s29c_runtime.oot` **no new ELF**;
`s29c_harness.oot` smoke **exit 1**). Fairy independently probed the
**rebuild**, not the hole again.

| Attempt | Result | Class |
|---------|--------|-------|
| Tree `oodac check oodac/main.oo` (20s) | rc=**124**, 0 bytes | SPRINT AST deadlock / AUDIT **R4** |
| Tree `emit-c c_emit_secret.oo` (45s) | rc=**124**, **4096** B (pipe page) | **same on HEAD and WT** — not the depth hunk |
| Tree `emit-c c_emit_secret_guard.oo` (30s) | rc=**124**, 4096 B | tree emit hang on this family |
| Tree `emit-c c_emit_print.oo` (30s) | rc=0, 11489 B | **print alone emits** |
| Tree `check c_emit_secret.oo` | rc=1 `undefined variable 'c_env_put'` in **4.1s** | standalone check is not the hang |
| Tree `tokens c_emit_secret.oo` | rc=0, 1707 toks, **2.65s** | lexer fine |
| **Seed** `emit-c c_emit_secret.oo` | rc=0, **18173** B, **6.09s** | C has `long long depth` in **both** walkers |
| **Seed** `emit-c c_emit_print.oo` | rc=0, 10580 B | C has `long long d` |
| `/tmp/oodac_build.log` | `ERR_EMIT_LINE check_caps.oo` / `OO_FLIGHT_RECORDER_LOG` | last tree `build` fail |
| `run_build.oo` | `./oodac/oodac build ooda/oodac/main.oo` | **tree host as emit host** — the dead path |

Live product host **unchanged**: 962960 B, md5 `a44ee35eb344837009697e2c9d4e4662`,
BuildID `a93cfd09…`, mtime 2026-08-12 04:49:59 **-1000** (= 07:49 PDT).
WT: `c_emit_print.oo` 97 L md5 `4a993a55…` (`d`); `c_emit_secret.oo` 231 L
md5 `b96bfc0e…` (`depth` + 7.10 slice + 2.10 `__sec_sink__`).

Dirty oodac is **11 files**, not two. A “rebuild the working tree” also
pulls 6.1 `check_drive`, 2.10 guard, R2 `load_import`, `lex`, `tc_names`.
That is why a naive seed multi of **tip dirt** is not a 2.9 ship.

**Two FN subclasses (still live on this ELF — do not collapse):**

| ID | Shape | ELF today |
|----|-------|-----------|
| **H-later** | `println((1), tok)` / `eprintln(id(1), tok)` | check/llvm/wasm FN; stmt emit-c BLOCK (outer arg) |
| **H-same** | `println(("x") + tok)` | check FN; stmt emit-c **leaks `tok`**; eprintln emit-c BLOCK |

Harness exact H-same is `("x") + tok`. Extra wrap `((("x")+tok))` is
`ERR	type` on this ELF — **not** a SECRET seal (`s29c_harness.oot`).

**Not this wave:** new walker, fake C `args`, `c_secret_emit_guard` from
check/stmt, AST-deadlock rewrite, IFC, `${}`, 2.10 wrappers, emit-bc.

## Constraints (hard)
1. **Path A only** — ship the **already-written** Int depth walks. Do not
   invent a third refuse machine.
2. **Rebuild-fail is proved.** Do not tell DE to `run_build.oo` / tree
   `oodac build main.oo` / tree `emit-c` of `c_emit_secret.oo`.
3. **Seed is the emit host** (`bootstrap/seed/oodac`, BuildID `7dcbc155…`).
   `SEED_PURE_MULTI.oot` + `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1` already exist. R4 says
   bootstrap **often needs** that skip.
4. **Isolate 2.9.** Overlay **print + secret depth** onto **HEAD**, not the
   11-file dirty tree. 6.1 / 2.10 / R2 are other IDs.
5. **Side binary first.** `$TMPDIR/s29c_oodac_depth` — never clobber
   `oodac/oodac` until I2 exit 0. **No ELF commit** (`s29c_hygiene.oot`).
6. **Do not greenwash** wave-1 ALREADY_FIXED or WT grep as FIXED.
7. **Both rails.** Print-only splice leaves check/llvm FN. Secret-only
   splice leaves H-same emit-c leak.
8. **One smoke.** Extend/prove `scripts/s29_println_guard_smoke.oo`
   (194 L). No second 2.9 script.
9. **Memory H3** still forbids `args = args + ", " + a`.
10. **Fairy writes ideas only.** DE owns isolate + link + prove.
11. **DEBT #18:** do not race a second `pure_build` against `ci_product`.

## Darwin scorecard (path-A residual)
Axes 0–10 (higher = survives compile cycle). Sum/5 ≈ rank:

| Axis | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Close** | Gets H-later + H-same dual `ERR	secret` on a **new** ELF |
| **Honest** | Names rebuild-fail; no “just rebuild the tip”; no emit_guard lie |
| **Smoke** | Cheap: existing s29 rails + Peer1 four MUST on **that** ELF |
| **Entropy** | Lowers \(S\) (stale host, WT-only depth, dirty-tree mix) |
| **Ship** | Uses seed + two files + skip-check; no deadlock fix; no new arch |

**Rule:** losers pruned. 1–2 winners advance to DE this turn.

---

## Ideas evaluated
### I1 — Seed-host **isolate** rebuild (HEAD + two depth files) ⭐
**Shape:** Do not self-host. Do not emit the dirty 11-file tree.

1. Worktree or `$TMPDIR/s29c_iso/` copy of `ooda/oodac/` at **HEAD**
   (`52cc4b5`).
2. Overlay **only**:
   - `c_emit_print.oo` WT (Int `d`, 87→97) — 2.9 stmt belt
   - `c_emit_secret.oo` — **prefer I3 cherry-pick** (depth only). If DE
     will not split the hunk, overlay whole WT 231 L and **name** 7.10
     `str_slice` + 2.10 `__sec_sink__` as riders (not 2.9 FIXED).
3. Emit host = `bootstrap/seed/oodac` (fairy: secret **6s**, print OK,
   depth present in C).
4. `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1 OODAC_BIN=<seed> bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build \
     oodac/main.oo $TMPDIR/s29c_oodac_depth`
   Same contract as `scripts/seed_pure_multi_smoke.oo` (side path).
5. Do **not** copy over `oodac/oodac` until I2 is green.

**Why this is the ship-now after rebuild-fail:** tree ELF cannot emit
`c_emit_secret.oo` (hang, HEAD **and** WT). Seed can. Isolate stops
`check_caps` / `OO_FLIGHT_RECORDER_LOG` / R2 / 6.1 from riding the 2.9
binary. `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1` walks around R4 / AST deadlock on `main.oo`.

**Darwin:** Close 10 · Honest 10 · Smoke 9 · Entropy 10 · Ship 9 → **avg 9.6**

### I2 — Prove the **side** ELF (same rails, new host) ⭐
**Shape:** `OODAC_BIN=$TMPDIR/s29c_oodac_depth` + virgin TMPDIR cwd.

| Gate | Expect |
|------|--------|
| Fingerprint | **new** size / md5 / BuildID — not `a44ee35e…` / `a93cfd09…` |
| Runtime nm | check walker LPAREN **≥ 2**; scan_call **5** token eqs; stmt loop LPAREN (`s29c_runtime.oot` list) |
| H-later | `println((1), tok)` check **and** emit-c `ERR	secret` |
| H-same | `println(("x") + tok)` check **and** emit-c `ERR	secret`; **no** `oo_print_*` operand `tok` |
| Peer1 #3 | `eprintln(id(1), tok)` check **and** emit-c `ERR	secret` |
| Control | `println(n, tok)` still dual SECRET; `println("tok")` no-FP |
| Smoke | `s29_println_guard_smoke.oo` **exit 0** on **that** ELF |
| Grep | **no** `c_secret_emit_guard` in print/secret; **no** `args = args +` in `c_emit_println` |

`ERR	type` is FAIL. Then — and only then — replace gitignored
`oodac/oodac`. Do **not** `git add` the ELF.

**Darwin:** Close 9 · Honest 10 · Smoke 10 · Entropy 10 · Ship 9 → **avg 9.6**

### I3 — Cherry-pick **depth only** onto HEAD `c_emit_secret.oo`
**Shape:** HEAD file is 259 L first-`)`. Copy the two Int `depth`
counters (scan_call + println/eprintln loop). Leave HEAD sink-list
and **omit** WT 7.10 / 2.10 / compress. Print overlay is already a
14-line 2.9-only diff.

**Darwin:** Close 8 · Honest 10 · Smoke 8 · Entropy 9 · Ship 8 → **avg 8.6**
**Why bundle with I1:** cleanest 2.9 binary. If cherry-pick slips,
I1 whole-file overlay + named riders is acceptable. Do **not** block
the ship on a pretty diff.

### I4 — Two-TU C splice (if isolate multi still fails)
**Shape:** Seed already emitted both TUs. Replace `c_emit_println` /
`c_secret_scan_call` / `check_secret_println_sinks` in a **HEAD**
seed `all.c`, gcc-link a side ELF.

**Darwin:** Close 8 · Honest 7 · Smoke 7 · Entropy 7 · Ship 6 → **avg 7.0**
**Why fallback, not first:** works if `pure_build` of HEAD+two dies on
an unrelated module. Manual splice is easy to mis-cut. Prefer I1.

### I5 — Print-only splice (tree emit of print **works**)
**Shape:** Relink only `c_emit_println` `d`. Leave check walker flat.

**Darwin:** Close 4 · Honest 5 · Smoke 5 · Entropy 3 · Ship 7 → **avg 4.8**
**Why not enough:** H-same emit-c would BLOCK. H-later/H-same **check
+ llvm + wasm stay FN**. Peer1 still REJECT. Wave-3 runtime gate is
the **check** LPAREN loop.

